#  'upcoming_deal_details': '<h3>Updates</h3>\n<p dir="ltr"><strong>26/09/22:</strong> The way you will access and use the digital tool for G-cloud 13 is changing.</p>\n<p dir="ltr">In summer 2022 we launched a new digital service called the Public Procurement Gateway (PPG). G-cloud is due to go live on PPG’s contract and award service on 9 November 2022.</p>\n<p dir="ltr">You will need to register for PPG to buy through it. For more information and instructions on how to register for PPG, <a href="https://assets.crowncommercial.gov.uk/wp-content/uploads/RM1557.13-Public-Procurement-Gateway-Information.odt" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://assets.crowncommercial.gov.uk/wp-content/uploads/RM1557.13-Public-Procurement-Gateway-Information.odt&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1664271807499000&amp;usg=AOvVaw234BnEezSdUhZK3ZppFbDQ">read the Public Procurement Gateway information document</a></p>\n<p><strong>26/08/22</strong> &#8211; CCS has taken the decision to vary the framework term of G-Cloud 12, meaning it will remain open for customers to call off from for two months after its current end date, until 27 November.</p>\n<p>This will ensure that customers can continue to buy the services they need and will give us the additional time to ensure that when G-Cloud 13 is launched on 9 November, it will deliver the best experience for customers and suppliers.</p>\n<p><span style="font-weight: 400;"><strong>03/08/2022:</strong> we have taken the difficult decision to delay the launch of GCloud 13. Buyers and suppliers can find out more by reading </span><a href="https://www.crowncommercial.gov.uk/news/digital-outcomes-g-cloud-an-update-for-ccs-customers-and-suppliers"><span style="font-weight: 400;">our news item</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;">. </span></p>\n<h3><b>Summary:\xa0</b></h3>\n<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Buy cloud-based computing services such as hosting, software and cloud support, including many off-the-shelf, pay-as-you-go cloud solutions.</span></p>\n<h3><b>Description:\xa0</b></h3>\n<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">G-Cloud 13 will replace </span><a href="https://www.crowncommercial.gov.uk/agreements/RM1557.12"><span style="font-weight: 400;">G-Cloud 12</span></a><span style="font-weight: 400;"> and will continue to provide cloud hosting and software services, together with associated support services to the UK central government departments and all other public sector bodies.</span></p>\n<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">We are introducing the following changes;</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style="font-weight: 400;">improved terms and conditions, with greater inclusion for the provision of day rate cloud support services</span></li>\n<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">inclusion of the latest procurement policies, including social value and prompt payment</span></li>\n<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">introduction of a fourth Lot for further competition for Cloud Support Services for larger, more complex requirements.</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Note, the scope and application process for Lots 1-3 remain unchanged. Suppliers can apply for any combination of the four lots</span><span style="font-weight: 400;">.</span></p>\n<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The G-Cloud 13 agreement will run for 12 months with an option to extend for a further 12 months.\xa0</span></p>\n<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">The G-Cloud 13 call-off term has changed to 36 months with an optional 12 month extension.</span></p>\n<h3><b>Benefits:\xa0</b></h3>\n<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">It is intended to build upon the benefits of the previous G-Cloud framework, including;</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">access to multiple suppliers and cloud services, including a high number of SMEs</span></li>\n<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">quick and easy route to market</span></li>\n<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">access to the latest cloud technology and innovation</span></li>\n<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="1"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Improved pricing via further competition for Cloud Support Services in Lot 4</span></li>\n</ul>\n<h3><b>Product types:\xa0</b></h3>\n<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Lot 1 Cloud Hosting (PaaS, IaaS) &#8211; cloud platform or infrastructure, which allows buyers to deploy, manage and run software, and provision and use processing, storage or networking resources;</span></p>\n<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Lot 2 Cloud Software (SaaS) &#8211; applications which are accessed over the internet and hosted in the cloud;</span></p>\n<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Lot 3 Cloud Support &#8211; </span><span style="font-weight: 400;">to help set up and maintain cloud software or hosting services.</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="2"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Cloud Migration Planning</span></li>\n<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="2"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Set Up and Migration</span></li>\n<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="2"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Security Services</span></li>\n<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="2"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Quality Assurance and Performance Testing</span></li>\n<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="2"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Training</span></li>\n<li style="font-weight: 400;" aria-level="2"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Ongoing Support</span></li>\n</ul>\n<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Lot 4 Cloud Support &#8211; Further Competition &#8211; the scope of this lot is the same as lot 3 but is designed for larger, more complex requirements procured through further competition.</span></p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<h3><b>Market engagement:</b></h3>\n<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">In 2021 we ran supplier and customer surveys. We later held a supplier event and 1 to 1 supplier interviews.\xa0</span></p>\n<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">We held customer events in June 2021. These events helped us to understand the details around needs for buying, consuming and implementing cloud services.\xa0</span></p>\n<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">In December 2021 CCS published a RFI to G-Cloud 12 lot 3 suppliers to obtain feedback on the scope and market interest for lot 4.\xa0</span></p>\n<p><span style="font-weight: 400;">Check this page often for updates on our plans for further engagement.</span></p>\n<h3><b>Important links</b></h3>\n<table style="width: 98.0927%;">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td style="width: 66.9725%;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Prior Information Notice (PIN)</span></td>\n<td style="width: 124.785%;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Not applicable</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style="width: 66.9725%;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Contract Notice in Find a Tender Service (FTS)</span></td>\n<td style="width: 124.785%;"><span style="font-weight: 400;"><a href="https://www.find-tender.service.gov.uk/Notice/006385-2022">Read contract notice for lots 1 to 3</a><br />\n<a href="https://www.find-tender.service.gov.uk/Notice/006384-2022">Read contract notice for lot 4</a></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style="width: 66.9725%;"><span style="font-weight: 400;">Tender documents</span></td>\n<td style="width: 124.785%;"><span style="font-weight: 400;"><a href="https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/52e2fd33-e6f3-4a4c-8697-d25ab76ea0a9">Download tender document for lots 1 to 3</a><br />\n<a href="https://www.contractsfinder.service.gov.uk/Notice/81ba3cce-1dbc-4484-a8c5-b22f72090d86">Download tender documents for lot 4</a></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<h3><b>Timeline</b></h3>\n<table>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><b>Activity</b></td>\n<td><b>Estimated dates</b></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span style="font-weight: 400;">Pre-market engagement</span></td>\n<td><span style="font-weight: 400;">August 2021</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span style="font-weight: 400;">Drafting of procurement documentation</span></td>\n<td><span style="font-weight: 400;">November 2021</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span style="font-weight: 400;">Publication of FTS notice</span></td>\n<td><span style="font-weight: 400;">8 March 2022</span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span style="font-weight: 400;">Framework Award</span></td>\n<td><span style="font-weight: 400;">TBC</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n',
